.TH qsh-config 1  "config 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-config \- Read and edit this machine\*(Aqs `config.toml` by dotted key (`docs/CLI.md` §6.23, ADR\-0051 decision 10)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh config\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read and edit this machine\*(Aqs `config.toml` by dotted key (`docs/CLI.md` §6.23, ADR\-0051 decision 10)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
qsh\-config\-get(1)
Print the value of one key. An unset key prints `(unset)` and exits 0; an unknown key is a usage error (`INVALID_ARGUMENT`)
.TP
qsh\-config\-set(1)
Write one key. The edited file must pass the same validation the daemons apply at startup, or nothing is written. Comments and key order in `config.toml` are kept
.TP
qsh\-config\-unset(1)
Remove one key so its built\-in default applies again
.TP
qsh\-config\-list(1)
List the keys `config.toml` sets
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
